(Title) Tj
T*
(Neurobiological mechanisms in psychological treatment of anxiety: protocol for a) Tj
T*
(randomized trial examining neurotrophic factor changes during acceptance-based versus) Tj
T*
(supportive psychotherapy) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Background: Psychological interventions produce clinical improvement in anxiety disorders,) Tj
T*
(but the underlying neurobiological mechanisms are incompletely understood. Neurotrophic) Tj
T*
(factors regulate neural plasticity and may represent a biomarker of therapeutic response.) Tj
T*
(Methods: This 14-week randomized trial will enroll 85 adults aged 18-65 with diagnosed) Tj
T*
(generalized anxiety disorder. Participants will be randomized 1:1 to either group) Tj
T*
(acceptance-based behavior therapy \(ABBT\) or supportive therapy \(ST\), each delivered across) Tj
T*
(10 sessions. Blood samples for plasma neurotrophic factor measurement will be collected at) Tj
T*
(baseline and post-treatment. Clinical anxiety severity will be assessed using standardized) Tj
T*
(rating scales. Participants will complete self-report measures of worry, anxiety symptoms,) Tj
T*
(and functional impairment. Correlations between neurotrophic factor changes and clinical) Tj
T*
(outcomes will be examined using Pearson correlation and linear regression analyses.) Tj
ET
